like-for-like: the timed kernel (bwt_inverse) follows the Crystal BWTDecode kernel step for step (byte counts, cumulative start positions, next-pointer table, then the walk from original_idx); the input is produced once, untimed, by the prefix-doubling forward transform (bwt_transform) instead of the Crystal encoder, so its code shape differs, but the timed decode and the checksum do not depend on how the forward transform is written. Prep mode runs only the warmup rounds.
